      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Differentiating the functional equation reflects a left-side derivative-zero problem into a gamma-factor or auxiliary-function problem. Boundary domination can transfer a zero count by Rouché, whereas quotienting the auxiliary function by zeta and applying Littlewood transfers horizontal displacement into a boundary norm; telescoping higher derivative ratios extends the latter route.",
